    "5": {
      "class_type": "MarkdownNote",
      "id": "5",
      "inputs": {
        "unused_widget_0": "# NovaSR - Quick Setup Guide\n\n## \ud83d\udcc1 Model Folder Structure\n\nCreate this folder in your ComfyUI installation:\n\n```\nComfyUI/\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 models/\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 NovaSR/\n        \u251c\u2500\u2500 pytorch_model.bin\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500 NovaSR.safetensors\n```\n\n## \ud83d\udce5 Download Models\n\n| Model | Download Link | Format | Size |\n|-------|---------------|---------|-------|\n| PyTorch | [pytorch_model.bin](https://huggingface.co/drbaph/NovaSR/resolve/main/pytorch_model.bin) | .bin | 53.2 KB |\n| SafeTensors | [NovaSR.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/drbaph/NovaSR/resolve/main/NovaSR.safetensors) | .safetensors | 48 KB |\n\n**[\u2192 View all models on HuggingFace](https://huggingface.co/drbaph/NovaSR/tree/main)**\n\n**Note:** Both formats contain the same model. Choose the one you prefer. SafeTensors is more secure and widely recommended.\n\n\n## \u2699\ufe0f Node Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Value | Description |\n|-----------|--------|-------------|\n| Audio | *(input)* | Connect Load Audio node output |\n| Model | `NovaSR.safetensors` | Model file to use |\n| Unload Model | `False` | Keep model in VRAM for faster repeats |\n| Show Spectrogram | `True` | Generate before/after comparison image |\n\n\n## \ud83d\udcdd Tips\n\n1. **Mono Output:** NovaSR is mono-only. Use a mono-to-stereo node after if you need stereo\n2. **Any Input:** Works with any sample rate - automatically resampled to 16kHz\n3. **Stereo Handling:** Stereo inputs are automatically mixed to mono (average of channels)\n4. **Batch Processing:** Model stays loaded for fast consecutive processing (unless \"Unload Model\" is checked)\n5. **Real-time Use:** So fast it can enhance audio in real-time during recording or playback\n\n## \ud83d\udd17 Links\n\n- [GitHub Repository](https://github.com/Saganaki22/ComfyUI-NovaSR)\n- [Models on HuggingFace](https://huggingface.co/drbaph/NovaSR)\n- [Original NovaSR Repo](https://github.com/ysharma3501/NovaSR)\n- [Original Paper](https://github.com/ysharma3501/NovaSR)\n\n**NovaSR provides comparable quality at 1/1000th the size and 6000x faster than AudioSR!**\n"
      },
